‹Heading1,b:Gleam›
‹Rule:────────────────────────────────────────›

Gleam turns a folder of Markdown into a
site. It has ‹Text,b:no runtime›, reads a single
‹Link,u:config file›, and builds a thousand pages
in under a second. See the ‹Link,u:changelog› and
the ‹Link,u:contributing guide›.

‹Image:󰥶 A screenshot of the generated site  ›‹ImageHost:g…›

‹Heading2,b:Install›

‹CodeFrame:╭─ ›‹CodeLang:sh›‹CodeFrame: ─────────────────────────────────╮›
‹CodeFrame:│ ›‹LineNumber:1 ›‹CodeText:go install example.com/gleam/cmd/…›‹CodeFrame: │›
‹CodeFrame:╰──────────────────────────────────────╯›

Or download a binary from the ‹Link,u:releases›
‹Link,u:page›. Contact ‹Link,u:mailto:hello@example.com›
or ‹Link,u:https://example.com/gleam› for help.

‹Heading2,b:Usage›

  ‹Bullet:1. ›Create ‹Code: gleam.toml ›
  ‹Bullet:2. ›Put pages in ‹Code: content/ ›
  ‹Bullet:3. ›Run ‹Code: gleam build ›

